  "2026-11-09T20:14:09.943Z",codex-agent,"The source-workspace privacy gate also passed: 9140 Git objects audited with approved identities and no secret or host-path findings. The focused contracts cover App-only landing, disabled repository auto-merge, absent/unknown base protection, parked-run URLs and the five-minute dispatch limit. Caller templates keep release SHA pins and existing configuration; adopting the fix requires their normal pin update."
  "2026-11-09T20:16:21.432Z",codex-agent,"Final local verification: focused contract command passed 117/117; NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"earlier armed auto-merge|previous auto-merge is revoked|ambiguous deliveries open\" test/closeout-workflow.test.ts passed all 11 selected tests with no skips. npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run lint and npm run changelog:check passed. Strict tracker health with --no-extensions passed (only pre-existing stale-item advisories). Extension-enabled local health is blocked by extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew:2026.11.4:2026.11.8:pm-github; no dependency pin changed. CI must certify the full gate on the pushed head. Revert proof is recorded above; no new upstream PM CLI or SDK defect was found."
  "2026-11-10T00:23:32.258Z",codex-agent,"Continuing PR #229 re-review on the existing branch. Verified the remote branch matches, origin/main is already merged, and both review findings are valid. General rules: informational reporting must not turn successful dispatch/auto-merge preparation into failure; regression contracts must reject runner-waiting operations independently of loop spelling. Audit both reusable workflows and all package polling/reporting paths, preserve working behavior, add adversarial tests and behavioral revert proofs, then run focused and full npm/Bun release gates with at most two workers."
  "2026-11-10T00:25:16.511Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: both reusable dispatch steps contained an unguarded informational parked-run lookup; both now discard partial failed output, emit a notice and exit successfully without retrying. Dispatch failures still fail closed before arming. Existing successful-report tests remain intact. The shared no-wait assertion now bans run watch/view (including whitespace and repository flags), check-runs/check-suites and PR checks --watch in both dispatch paths; 14 adversarial cases cover while/until/for spellings. Package-wide audit: closeout SDK check-runs is a single paginated evidence read, CLI/SDK import sleeps are API retry/local lock contention, release.yml waits concern package publication and is not reusable; none waits for caller runner capacity. JSON/TOON and packed npm/Bun/non-git trackers have no separate dispatch/report implementation: these workflows are repository assets, not shipped npm files, and are intrinsically git-based. No unrelated product-path edits were needed. Focused workflow suite: 135/135 pass."
  "2026-11-10T00:25:17.934Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy (the package worktree remained fixed): node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"parked-run listing failure\" test/bot-pr-workflow.test.ts fails 4/4 after restoring only both dispatch blocks from e4e9eea, retaining all new tests. Restoring fixed workflows and removing only the strengthened polling-command assertion makes node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"no-wait contract rejects adversarial polling\" test/bot-pr-workflow.test.ts fail 14/14. Restoring the assertion passes the combined selection 18/18 with zero failures. Both review classes have tests that fail on revert."
  "2026-11-10T00:26:16.827Z",codex-agent,"Audit clarification: release.yml is outside the reusable-workflow scope, but its own release-PR merge loop does wait for release checks; only its later sleeps concern registry propagation. This distinct publication continuation contract is recorded as a separate follow-up rather than changing release behavior in PR #229. The existing closed release wait-budget item is historical, not an open fix. The linked new regression selection also passed through pinned pm test --run --progress with schema/source context in a scratch tracker: 18/18; no run artifacts were written into this package tracker."
  "2026-11-10T00:52:50.932Z",codex-agent,"The first full npm release gate reached the closeout workflow suite and exposed one existing fixture that classified RUN_LIST_DENIED as a fatal maintenance failure. Stopped that known-failing run before the Bun gate. Kept the existing exit-1 and revocation assertions intact and moved its injected failure to the required production head-SHA lookup (missing fixture ref, normalized exit 1). Added an end-to-end informational failure test executing the real workflow plus always cleanup against a packed consumer: lookup failure exits 0, reports once, keeps armed auto-merge and never disables it. Focused maintenance plus informational tests pass 2/2. In a disposable full source copy, restoring only the old closeout dispatch block fails the new cleanup test 1/1; restored source passes. Full gates will be rerun after this correction."
  "2026-11-10T00:52:53.740Z",codex-agent,"The separate release-PR runner-wait follow-up is pm-github-sgyr; its implementation is outside reusable sync/closeout and no release behavior was changed. Review mapping: PRR_kwDOTbN4pM8AAAABW6t-ZA outside-diff report finding is covered in both workflows and the packed closeout cleanup regression; PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM61ctZ7 is covered by the shared polling-command assertion and 14 adversarial tests."
  "2026-11-10T01:55:42.414Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passed with an isolated HOME/global Git configuration and credential-free public npm environment. Node test runner concurrency remained 2: 1800 passed, 0 failed, 2 existing SDK lifecycle-compensation skips tied to pm-cli#1656 (1802 total). Coverage gate measured all 30 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100. Typecheck/build/docstrings/lint, zero duplication, identity/privacy audit, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry-run, changelog check and publication attestation passed. The informational cleanup and corrected required-head failure tests both passed inside the full gate. The Bun release gate is running sequentially on the same implementation; no thresholds or skips were changed."
  "2026-11-10T03:10:40.120Z",codex-agent,"The Bun full test phase finished: 1799 passed, 1 failed, 2 existing SDK lifecycle-compensation skips. Every workflow/re-review regression passed, including informational lookup cleanup and fatal required-head lookup revocation. The only failure is an unchanged built-package selector CLI package-install setup returning null under its existing 45-second subprocess bound; npm full passed that case, and an isolated instrumented recheck passed 1/1 with the same deadline and assertions. Evidence is attached to the existing intermittent packed-fixture item pm-github-r14n. No root resource/registry cause is established, no tests or deadlines were weakened, and this Bun run will not be represented as green. Coverage reporting is completing before final cleanup and push."
  "2026-11-10T03:32:13.981Z",codex-agent,"Final re-review validation: npm run release:check exited 0 (1800 passed, 0 failed, 2 existing pm-cli#1656 skips; exact coverage across 30 authored modules). bun run release:check exited 1 (1799 passed, 1 unchanged selector package-install setup failure, 2 existing SDK skips); its raw coverage summary is complete but does not make the failed gate green. The isolated selector test passed 1/1 under instrumentation with unchanged limits; details remain in pm-github-r14n. Separately, bun run audit:prod, bun run pack:dry-run, bun run changelog:check and bun run verify:release-publish-attestation all exited 0. Focused workflow contracts passed 135/135; focused cleanup/maintenance passed 2/2; reporting, polling-command and real cleanup revert controls fail 4/4, 14/14 and 1/1 respectively, with fixed controls passing. All tests used at most two workers, no threshold/assertion was weakened, no test/watch process remains active, and origin/main was refreshed and remains an ancestor. Both requested findings are fixed; the inline thread remains open for reviewer verification. The release-publication continuation is separately tracked in pm-github-sgyr. Releasing this claim without closing the item; the same PR will receive the fix commit and re-review request. Fresh pushed-head CI remains required."
  "2026-11-10T05:05:44.748Z",pi-github228-1109,"Re-review round 2 (PR 229) posted 2 additional comments outside the diff. Class rule: an armed-state flag must record an observed successful arm, never an intention. The only instance in the package is CLOSEOUT_AUTOMERGE_ALLOWED in the closeout dispatch step, which is set whenever an App deadline exists even when enable_auto_merge fell back (disabled setting, missing protection, or a failed gh pr merge). A request armed by an earlier step in the same run would then survive the always() revoke step. Fix: the flag is written only after the arm call succeeds, and the function returns a status so every fallback path is explicit. The Dependabot merge script already returns armed only after a verified request, so no second instance exists. The other outside-diff note (gh api preflight timeouts) is the reviewer's own design note marked no change required: both calls already sit inside the step's 5-minute timeout, and adding per-call timeouts would only duplicate that bound."
  "2026-11-10T05:16:00.116Z",pi-github228-1109,"Round 2 outside-diff fix: the closeout armed flag now records only an observed successful arm. enable_auto_merge returns 0 only after the arm call itself succeeds and 1 on every fallback (no App deadline, disabled or unverifiable repository setting, absent or unverifiable branch protection, failed gh pr merge). The shared shell captures that status before any later command, and the closeout-only block writes CLOSEOUT_AUTOMERGE_ALLOWED only when the status is true, so the always() cleanup revokes any request armed earlier in the same run instead of skipping it. The sync shell stays byte-identical apart from the closeout hold and flag block. Revert proof: replacing the flag condition with the old deadline check makes all 5 failed-arm cases in test/bot-pr-workflow.test.ts fail; restoring it makes all 6 armed-flag cases pass. The Dependabot merge script already returns armed only after a verified request, so the class has no second instance. The other outside-diff note (gh api preflight timeouts) is the reviewer's own design note marked no change required; both calls already sit inside the step's 5-minute timeout."
  "2026-11-10T05:16:57.829Z",pi-github228-1109,"Pushed 223e6c7 to the existing PR 229 and requested a fresh CodeRabbit review. Both outside-diff findings are answered in the PR: the armed-flag class is fixed with a revert-proven regression, and the gh api preflight note is the reviewer's own design note requiring no change. Focused gates: bot-pr-workflow 79/79, closeout auto-merge/parked-run/ambiguous subset 12/12, workflow contract suites 69/69, typecheck clean, changelog:check clean. The full release gate stays with CI on the pushed head."
  "2026-11-10T13:54:56.531Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator fix: CI failed in tsc (test/bot-pr-workflow.test.ts(103,38) TS2769: env.GITHUB_ENV is string | undefined). The agent's local release:check passed on stale node_modules; a clean npm ci (@types/node 26.6.6, typescript 7.0.2) reproduces it. The read is now guarded with if (env.GITHUB_ENV). tsc -p tsconfig.test.json clean, lint clean, test/bot-pr-workflow.test.ts 79/0. The full suite could not finish locally under load 13-17 on 4 cores (killed at 50 min), so CI certifies the full gate."
